        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161273586?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #20177.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1357608893\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/20177\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/20177/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/20177\">#20177</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The guide only mentions Emscripten, which led to the request for a pointer to lighter, more portable alternatives. Per the discussion on the issue (<a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/Josh-Cena/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/Josh-Cena\">@Josh-Cena</a> and <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/bsmth/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/bsmth\">@bsmth</a>), the consensus was to keep the tutorial primarily Emscripten-based but add a note about alternatives in the introduction — so this adds a short note pointing to compiling C directly with Clang/LLVM or the WASI SDK, while noting what Emscripten provides that those don't (libc, file system, and other OS emulation).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The Clang/LLVM reference is the <a href=\"https://surma.dev/things/c-to-webassembly/\" rel=\"nofollow\">surma.dev write-up</a> <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/bsmth/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/bsmth\">@bsmth</a> linked in the thread.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44351",
            "title": "Note alternatives to Emscripten in C to Wasm guide",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-04T01:29:51.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-04T01:28:08.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "vamshikrishnaramasamy",
                "url": "https://github.com/vamshikrishnaramasamy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161273586?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #20368.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1363933918\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/20368\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/20368/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/20368\">#20368</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The page mentions that open connections receive a <code class=\"notranslate\">versionchange</code> event, but doesn't explain the consequence: the deletion will not complete (and <code class=\"notranslate\">success</code> will not fire) while any connection to the database is still open. This is a common source of confusion — people wait for <code class=\"notranslate\">onsuccess</code> that never comes because a connection is left open.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This expands the existing sentence to spell out that:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>the deletion stays pending until every connection closes;</li>\n<li>a <code class=\"notranslate\">blocked</code> event is fired on the request if a connection doesn't close in response to <code class=\"notranslate\">versionchange</code>;</li>\n<li>closing connections (e.g. via <code class=\"notranslate\">IDBDatabase.close()</code>) lets the deletion proceed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This matches the <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/IndexedDB/#delete-a-database\" rel=\"nofollow\">spec's database-deletion steps</a> and the behavior <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/evanstade/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/evanstade\">@evanstade</a> quoted on the issue.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44350",
            "title": "Clarify that deleteDatabase() blocks until open connections close",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-04T01:25:19.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-04T01:23:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "vamshikrishnaramasamy",
                "url": "https://github.com/vamshikrishnaramasamy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161273586?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42933.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3860235982\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42933\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42933/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42933\">#42933</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">isConnected</code> always returns <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> on an {{domxref(\"Attr\")}} node, even when the attribute's <code class=\"notranslate\">ownerElement</code> is connected to the document. This trips people up, so this adds a note explaining why.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/caugner/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/caugner\">@caugner</a> noted on the issue, this is consistent across Chrome, Firefox, and Safari, and is out of scope for BCD — the spec defines <code class=\"notranslate\">isConnected</code> for all nodes, and since an attribute node has no parent, it has no root that is a document, so it is never \"connected\".</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I confirmed the behavior in Chrome:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"const el = document.createElement(&quot;div&quot;);\nel.setAttribute(&quot;data-x&quot;, &quot;1&quot;);\nconst attr = el.getAttributeNode(&quot;data-x&quot;);\ndocument.body.appendChild(el);\n\nel.isConnected;                 // true\nattr.ownerElement.isConnected;  // true\nattr.isConnected;               // false\nattr.parentNode;                // null\nattr.getRootNode() === attr;    // true (its root is itself, not the document)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">el</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">document</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">createElement</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"div\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">el</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">setAttribute</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"data-x\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-s\">\"1\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">attr</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">el</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">getAttributeNode</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"data-x\"</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">document</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">body</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">appendChild</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">el</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">el</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">isConnected</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>                 <span class=\"pl-c\">// true</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">attr</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">ownerElement</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">isConnected</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>  <span class=\"pl-c\">// true</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">attr</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">isConnected</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>               <span class=\"pl-c\">// false</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">attr</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">parentNode</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>                <span class=\"pl-c\">// null</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">attr</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">getRootNode</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">===</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">attr</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>    <span class=\"pl-c\">// true (its root is itself, not the document)</span></pre></div>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44349",
            "title": "Note that Attr.isConnected is always false",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-04T01:24:22.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-04T01:22:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "vamshikrishnaramasamy",
                "url": "https://github.com/vamshikrishnaramasamy"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This change adds links to the new script-on-click example in various places where background scripts and activeTab permission are documented.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The example is being made available in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4575503031\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/webextensions-examples/issues/636\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/webextensions-examples/pull/636/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/webextensions-examples/pull/636\">mdn/webextensions-examples#636</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44348",
            "title": "Add-reference references to the script-on-click example",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-03T23:34:16.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-03T23:32:29.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/538020?u=7619e27f6a00fc9753162c9c00e42501bc32c0ed&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Remove <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;form&gt;</code> elements from around <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;button&gt;</code>s in example HTML code.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Having <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;button&gt;</code> elements with <code class=\"notranslate\">id</code> attributes in an example's HTML code will break if they are inside a <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;form&gt;</code> element, because in addition to running the bound <code class=\"notranslate\">click</code> event handler, clicking the button will also attempt to submit the form,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This then results in a \"400 Bad Request\" error response from the playground <code class=\"notranslate\">runner.html</code> page, and the rendered demo promptly vanishes.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There's no need for the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;form&gt;</code> elements anyway, as <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;button&gt;</code> elements with event handlers bound to respond to <code class=\"notranslate\">click</code> events are functional on their own.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that only one of these examples was actually affected. (The second one didn't have an <code class=\"notranslate\">id</code> attribute on the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;button&gt;</code> element, so the form would not submit when clicked.) Nevertheless, I chose to remove the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;form&gt;</code> from both examples, because it still amounts to superfluous and unnecessary noise. Examples should be minimal for clarity.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/44346",
            "title": "CSS: style property page: Remove form elements from examples",
            "date_modified": "2026-06-03T19:41:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-06-03T19:24:37.000Z",
